    "name": "bounded_depth_listener",
    "hypothesis": "Listeners interpret referring expressions with a strictly bounded reasoning depth, inverting a communicative speaker who reasons about literal semantics rather than engaging in higher-order recursive mental simulation. This bounded depth prevents over-implicature, naturally preserving non-zero probability for multi-feature scalar competitors while strongly favoring minimal referents when words are universally shared. On uninformative displays without an informative word, visual attention defaults to contextually unique singletons.",
    "source": "round 2 candidate 2 explore"
   },
