    "name": "grammatical_exhaustification_distinct",
    "hypothesis": "Refining grammatical_exhaustification by incorporating continuous contextual distinctiveness into the visual attention prior: listeners interpret referring expressions through grammatical exhaustification over unasserted alternative features, ruling out referents proportionally to the informativeness of any more specific descriptions the speaker omitted, while spontaneous visual attention weights referents by combining discrete singleton salience with continuous feature contrast (contextual distinctiveness) relative to display competitors. This directly improves the representation of displays lacking identical duplicates as well as empty singletons in full-duplicate contexts, addressing the empirical discrepancy where humans allocate substantial prior belief to empty singleton objects among identical full-feature duplicates. Differences from grammatical_exhaustification: recursion depth remains unchanged (depth 0, L_exh); parameter w_distinct is added with prior dist.Normal(0.0, 1.0); no parameters are removed; and the visual prior is extended by adding w_distinct times the total contextual feature contrast (summed Hamming distance across all context objects).",
    "source": "round 2 candidate 6 refine chosen"
   },
   {
    "name": "rsa_l1_singleton_feat_color_valence_l0",
    "hypothesis": "RSA pragmatic listener at depth 1 with singleton salience, contextual distinctiveness, visual feature complexity, evaluative valence framing, visual color contrast, and literal L0. Refining rsa_l2_singleton_feat_color_valence_l0 by reducing pragmatic recursion depth from depth 2 to depth 1: listeners interpret referring expressions by inverting an informative speaker who evaluates literal semantics, rather than engaging in higher-order recursive mental simulation. This bounded depth eliminates over-implicature in scalar implicature and prevents multiplicative prior compounding across reasoning tiers, preserving appropriate probability on multi-feature competitors while maintaining common knowledge of visual singleton salience, continuous contextual distinctiveness, valence-modulated feature complexity, and color contrast. Differences from rsa_l2_singleton_feat_color_valence_l0: recursion depth is reduced from depth 2 to depth 1 (listener calls L1 instead of L2), the depth-2 listener memo L2 is removed, and all parameters (alpha, w_singleton, w_distinct, w_features, w_valence, w_color) are preserved without addition or removal.",
    "source": "round 2 candidate 4 refine incumbent rsa_l2_singleton_feat_color_valence_l0 retry 1 repair 1"
